{"id": "20473675", "revid": "9784415", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20473675", "title": "Dominique Dord", "text": "Dominique Dord (born 1 September 1959 in Chamb\u00e9ry, Savoie) is a French politician of the French Republican Party who served as a member of the National Assembly of France between 1997 and 2017. He represented the Savoie department, He is also the mayor of Aix-les-Bains since 2001.\nIn the Republicans\u2019 2016 presidential primaries, Dort endorsed Fran\u00e7ois Fillon as the party's candidate for the office of President of France.\nDominique Dord is a graduate of the Jean Moulin University Lyon 3 and HEC Paris."}
