{"id": "20473917", "revid": "35936988", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20473917", "title": "Fran\u00e7ois Goulard", "text": "Fran\u00e7ois Goulard (; born 21 September 1953 in Vannes) was a member of the National Assembly of France. He represented the Morbihan department, and is a member of the Union for a Popular Movement. He has been appointed as minister of transports from 2004 to 2005 and minister of superior education from 2005 to 2007.\nIn November 2021, he became treasurer of Horizons, a party within President Emmanuel Macron's Ensemble Citoyens coalition."}
